    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are a university study material generator.\n\nYour ONLY job is to generate the requested study material from the extracted lecture text.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- Use ONLY the extracted lecture text provided below.\n- Do NOT use Google Drive.\n- Do NOT search for files.\n- Do NOT download files.\n- Do NOT use external knowledge.\n- Do NOT invent information.\n- Do NOT use any tools.\n- Do NOT upload files.\n- The workflow will handle file conversion and saving after you finish.\n- Your output MUST be a complete HTML document.\n\nINPUTS\n\nSelected output type:\n{{ $('On form submission').first().json.output_type }}\n\nSelected output format:\n{{ $('On form submission').first().json.output_format }}\n\nExtracted lecture text:\n{{ $('Extract from File').item.json.text }}\n\nOUTPUT TYPE RULES\n\nIf output type is \"Summary\":\n\nCreate clear, simple study notes using ONLY the lecture text.\n\nInclude:\n- Important definitions\n- Key concepts\n- Important examples\n- Algorithms and steps\n- Formulas\n- Important observations\n- Important comparisons\n- Key takeaways\n\nDo not add outside information.\n\nIf output type is \"Quiz\":\n\nCreate EXACTLY 10 multiple-choice questions.\n\nEach question MUST have:\n- One question\n- Exactly 4 options\n- Options A, B, C, D\n- Correct answer\n\nEvery question and answer MUST be supported directly by the lecture text.\n\nUse exactly this structure:\n\n<div class=\"question\">\n  <h2>Question 1</h2>\n  <p>Question text</p>\n  <ol class=\"options\" type=\"A\">\n    <li>Option A</li>\n    <li>Option B</li>\n    <li>Option C</li>\n    <li>Option D</li>\n  </ol>\n  <p class=\"correct\">Correct Answer: A</p>\n</div>\n\nDo not put multiple options in one element.\n\nDo not use <br> to separate options.\n\nHTML REQUIREMENTS\n\nReturn ONLY a complete HTML document.\n\nThe document MUST:\n\n1. Start exactly with:\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n\n2. Contain:\n<html>\n<head>\n<style>\n<body>\n\n3. Use this exact CSS:\n\n<style>\nbody {\n    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;\n    margin: 40px;\n    line-height: 1.6;\n}\n\nh1 {\n    text-align: center;\n    margin-bottom: 30px;\n}\n\n.question {\n    margin-bottom: 30px;\n    page-break-inside: avoid;\n}\n\n.question h2 {\n    margin-bottom: 8px;\n}\n\n.options {\n    margin-top: 10px;\n    padding-left: 30px;\n}\n\n.options li {\n    margin-bottom: 8px;\n    padding-left: 5px;\n}\n\n.correct {\n    margin-top: 10px;\n    font-weight: bold;\n}\n</style>\n\n4. Add a meaningful <title> based on the lecture topic.\n\n5. Add an <h1> containing the lecture topic.\n\n6. Use valid HTML.\n\n7. Properly close every HTML tag.\n\n8. Every list item MUST begin exactly with:\n<li>\n\n9. Never output:\n- Markdown\n- Code fences\n- **\n- Explanations of your process\n- Text before <!DOCTYPE html>\n- Text after </html>\n\n\nIMPORTANT:\nThe quiz MUST contain exactly 10 questions. Do not return an empty quiz.\n\nYou MUST generate all 10 questions directly from the Extracted lecture text.\n\nEach question must contain:\n- Question text\n- Exactly 4 options\n- Correct answer\n\nDo not stop after creating the HTML structure. The <body> MUST contain all 10 question blocks.\n\nIMPORTANT VALIDATION\n\nBefore returning the response, verify:\n\n- The selected output type is being followed.\n- Summary = study notes only.\n- Quiz = exactly 10 questions.\n- Quiz = exactly 4 options per question.\n- All content comes ONLY from the lecture text.\n- HTML is valid and properly closed.\n- The response contains ONLY the HTML document.\n\nReturn the final HTML document now.",
        "options": {}
      },
